<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australia's SAFA says 97/98 funding A$1.0 bln.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australia's SAFA says 97/98 funding A$1.0 bln.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The South Australian Government Financing Authority (SAFA) said on Monday its funding requirement for 1997/98 will be around A$1.0 billion.  </p>
<p>The requirement was around the level seen for 1996/97 (July-June) and essentially related to the refinancing of maturing debt.</p>
<p>SAFA said this reflected the impact of the state government's debt reduction polices (including asset sales), the ongoing rundown of SAFA's financial asset holdings, and funding arising from the wind-down by SAFA of the treasury operations of the South Australian Asset Management Corporation (SAAMC).  </p>
<p>The following is a broad indication of sources of funding that may be utilised by SAFA in 1997/98.</p>
<p> DOMESTIC		(A$ million)</p>
<p> Commercial Paper    nil-200</p>
<p> Fixed Interest	200-400</p>
<p> CPI Linked	    nil</p>
<p> OFFSHORE		(A$ million equivalent)</p>
<p> Commercial Paper    200-400</p>
<p> Longer Term Issues  200-400</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
